# meta: !!omap
# - comments: ['Per-(detector, filter) placement CORRECTIONS onto the JWST 2-micron consensus frame.', dx_mas/dy_mas are the correction
#       to ADD -- the NEGATIVE of the measured, '  (filter - anchor) residual.  Applying the residual doubles the error.', 'frame=instrument:
#       sky vector rotated by +ROLL_REF; rotate by -ROLL_REF to apply', '  (filter_frame_correction.instrument_to_sky).', 'Module-mean
#       removed per module, after negation.', 'F182M: mean of three observations -- brick jw02221-o001 (ROLL_REF 89.13),', '  sgrc jw04147-o012
#       (91.50), wd2 jw03523-o005 (141.01).  A table built from', '  brick+sgrc alone predicts wd2 -- held out, 52 deg away in roll --
#       with 0.41 mas', '  residual and 95 percent of the variance explained; the opposite rotation gives', '  2.15 mas and explains nothing.',
#     'F187N: brick jw02221-o001 only (n=1).  Jay Anderson has no F187N STDGDC solution', '  and no second observation has been solved.  Residual
#       amplitude 0.55 mas.', 'Solved by scripts/analysis/solve_filter_frame_offsets.py --write; see issue #296.']
